    {
      "id": "graph-organization-overview",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Graph Organization Law",
      "position": {
        "x": -260,
        "y": -500
      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 240,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Graph Organization Law\n\nGraph Standardization owns the **invariant executable core**. This task owns the **composition layer**: practical authoring patterns that keep functioning graphs understandable as they grow and recognizable enough to become templates.\n\nThe deliverables are concrete:\n- section and header grammar\n- semantic and operational edge guidance\n- a template lens for recognizing reusable graph shapes\n- safe reorganization operations and scalable collections\n- template-library organization",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "markdown",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "identity": {
            "graphId": "markdown_class",
            "name": "markdown Node Class",
            "version": "0.1.0",
            "description": "Canonical markdown content node.",
