        "title": "Implement lean template installation",
        "body": "Copy a template's bounded functional nodes and edges into an existing graph, add the required bridges, preserve the host declaration and canonical root, rely on existing automatic graph rules, and reject ID collisions without suffixing.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "estimateHours": "4",
        "ideaRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/installing-templates-into-existing-graphs.node",
        "progressNote": "Complete. The bounded Workboard capability installs while preserving the host declaration and root. Workboard singleton collisions are rejected, and the first exact duplicate-ID test stopped without suffixing.",
        "completedCriteria": [
          "A bounded template capability installs into an existing graph",
          "The host declaration and canonical root remain unchanged",
          "Required bridges are added with the installed nodes",
          "Existing dependency, view, layout, and save behavior remains authoritative",
          "A second Workboard controller is rejected as a singleton capability collision",
          "An ID collision stops installation clearly and never creates a suffixed ID"
        ],
